                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90 h 12Anti-War/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2908</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s No. 272
                    of August 16, midnight, please send to the Minister of Afghanistan at Paris a
                    note as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I am instructed by my Government to send to you, for transmission to
                            your Government, two authenticated copies of the Multilateral Treaty for
                            the Renunciation of War, signed at Paris on August 27, last, one copy
                            being for the archives of your Government and the other for its use
                            should it so desire, in its formal adherence.</p>
                        <p>“I am also instructed by my Government to furnish, for the information of
                            your Government, a copy of a circular instruction to the diplomatic
                            agents of the United States accredited to Governments other than the
                            original signatories of the Treaty, dated September 17, 1928.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank B. Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
